    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.is_subgraph_isomorphic - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.is_subgraph_isomorphic.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_subgraph_isomorphic()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a pattern graph occurs inside this graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_subgraph_isomorphic()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a pattern graph occurs inside this graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.is_subgraph_isomorphic()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if a pattern graph occurs inside this graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if a pattern graph occurs inside this graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L21904-L22027){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.is_subgraph_isomorphic(\n    pattern,\n    induced=True,\n    node_attr=None,\n    edge_attr=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Is subgraph isomorphic](../assets/graphs/is-subgraph-isomorphic.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Each side searches graph g, a triangle A, B, C, for pattern p, a path of three nodes. Left: with induced=False extra edges are allowed, so the path maps onto B–A and B–C (in the accent color) and is_subgraph_isomorphic(p, induced=False) returns True. Right: with the default induced=True the matched nodes may have no extra edge, but the edge A–C (in the accent color) closes every candidate path into the triangle, so is_subgraph_isomorphic(p) returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA pattern occurs when its nodes can be matched to distinct nodes of this graph so that\nevery pattern edge corresponds to an edge here. With `induced=True` (the default), the\nmatched nodes must also have no *extra* edges among them, so the pattern appears as an\ninduced subgraph: a path of three nodes then does not occur inside a triangle. With\n`induced=False`, extra edges are allowed (a *monomorphism*), so any pattern whose edges\ncan be found is reported. Searching for small patterns is how motifs, functional\ngroups in molecules, fraud patterns in transaction graphs, or forbidden structures in\na design are found.\n\nBoth graphs must have the same directedness. Parallel edges and self-loops in the\npattern must be matched by the same number of edges (`induced=True`) or at least as\nmany (`induced=False`).\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[pattern]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The `Graph` to search for. It is not modified.\n\n<code>[induced]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), require an induced subgraph; if `False`, allow extra edges.\n\n<code>[node_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | list[str] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional node attribute name, or list of names, whose values must be equal for\n    matched nodes.\n\n<code>[edge_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | list[str] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional edge attribute name, or list of names, whose values must be equal for\n    matched edges.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if at least one occurrence exists.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If one graph is directed and the other is not.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe search is the VF2++ style backtracking used by `is_isomorphic()`, mapping the\npattern into this graph and stopping at the first occurrence. Subgraph isomorphism is\nNP-complete in general, but small patterns are found quickly. NetworkX's\n`GraphMatcher(G, pattern).subgraph_is_isomorphic()` and `subgraph_is_monomorphic()`\nanswer the same questions.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~subgraph_isomorphisms`) \n\n:   List the occurrences rather than test for one.\n\n[](`~largest_common_subgraph`) \n\n:   The largest part of a pattern that does occur.\n\n[](`~is_isomorphic`) \n\n:   Compare two whole graphs.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA triangle contains a path of three nodes as a subgraph, but not as an *induced*\nsubgraph, since the third edge of the triangle closes the path:\n\n::: {#b3f90bba .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ntriangle = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(3)\npath = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(3)\n\ntriangle.is_subgraph_isomorphic(path), triangle.is_subgraph_isomorphic(path, induced=False)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(False, True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nA square does contain the path as an induced subgraph:\n\n::: {#ab2febf0 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(4).is_subgraph_isomorphic(path)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Which molecules contain a benzene ring\n\nWith benzene itself as the pattern, each of `molecules()` is checked for a ring of six\natoms, then for a ring of six carbons (`node_attr=\"element\"`), then for a ring of six\ncarbons with aromatic bonds (adding `edge_attr=\"bond\"`):\n\n::: {#fe03c012 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport polars as pl\n\nmolecules = ec.molecules()\nbenzene = molecules[\"benzene\"]\n\npl.DataFrame(\n    [\n        {\n            \"molecule\": name,\n            \"six_ring\": molecule.is_subgraph_isomorphic(benzene),\n            \"carbons\": molecule.is_subgraph_isomorphic(benzene, node_attr=\"element\"),\n            \"aromatic\": molecule.is_subgraph_isomorphic(\n                benzene, node_attr=\"element\", edge_attr=\"bond\"\n            ),\n        }\n        for name, molecule in molecules.items()\n    ]\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (7, 4)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>molecule</th><th>six_ring</th><th>carbons</th><th>aromatic</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>bool</td><td>bool</td><td>bool</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;benzene&quot;</td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;cyclohexane&quot;</td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;ethanol&quot;</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;dimethyl_ether&quot;</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;butane&quot;</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;isobutane&quot;</td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;caffeine&quot;</td><td>true</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nCyclohexane has the ring of carbons, but with single bonds. Caffeine has a ring of six,\nbut two of its atoms are nitrogens:\n\n::: {#be5dbc0f .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncaffeine = molecules[\"caffeine\"]\nring = list(caffeine.subgraph_isomorphisms(benzene, limit=1)[0].values())\n\ncaffeine.plot(color_by=\"element\", highlight=ring + ring[:1], label_by=\"label\", seed=1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"fals